    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "",
    "lawSection": "Rockland County",
    "memo": "\n \nBILL NUMBER: S5948\n\nSPONSOR: SKOUFIS\n \nTITLE OF BILL:  An act authorizing the commissioner of general\nservices to transfer and convey certain unappropriated state land to\nRockland Recovery Homes, Inc.\n\n \nPURPOSE:\n\nThis bill would authorize the transfer of land from the office of gener-\nal services to Rockland Recovery Homes, Inc.\n\n \nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\n\nSection one of the bill authorizes the Commissioner of General Services\nto transfer and convey to Rockland Recovery Homes, Inc state land\ndescribed and shall be made in consideration of the sum of one dollar.\n\nSection two of the bill describes the location and coordinates of the\nland to be transferred and conveyed.\n\nSection three of the bill states that Rockland Recovery Homes, Inc may\nbe required to submit to the Commissioner of General Services an accu-\nrate survey and description of the land.\n\nSection four of the bill states that Rockland Recovery Homes, Inc must\ncomplete an application for the land within one year after the effective\ndate of this act.\n\nSection five describes use restrictions for the land.\n\nSection six of the bill relates to the effective date.\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nThis legislation will allow Rockland Recovery Homes, Inc to build a new\nfacility to serve as a recovery home for persons recovering from\naddiction.\n\n \nLEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\nNew bill.\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\n\nNone.\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nThis act shall take effect immediately.\n",
